# Exercise: Absolute Value
#
# `abs` returns the absolute value of an integer. It's part of
# the `std:imath` module, so you have to `include std:imath` at
# the top of the file to bring it into scope.
#
# After the include, the word is just `abs` — no `imath.` prefix.
#
# Example:
#   -42 abs    # Stack: ( 42 )
#   5 abs      # Stack: ( 5 )
#
# Your task: Implement a word that returns the absolute difference
# between two numbers.
#
# When done, delete the marker line below.

include std:imath

